A||N||8||Babygirl||Cam shaft pully and hub removal||||4||
Z||000000||Babygirl||09-18-2000||09:46 PM||||Help!  My '84 SE stopped working today!  I believe the problem is the cam shaft - it won't turn.  So I tried to remove the pully and it won't budge.  Does anyone know how to remove it?  OR at least which way do the threads turn?  IT won't move either way, and the Chilton's book doesn't say.  <P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||4
Z||000001||rnoswal||09-18-2000||10:05 PM||||Sorry to hear about your troubles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> . Just one question, do you know if the crank will turn any? Can you see the crankshaft rock back and forth just a little with the little play there is in the cam to crank gear? If not, then it may be more serious, like a spun rod bearing. Either way, the engine has to come out! <P><P>------------------<BR>Russ||||reg||9
Z||000002||Brian84SE||09-18-2000||10:54 PM||||The camshaft gear is pressed on.  The whole cam has to be removed to get it off.  Although camshaft gears strip out, what brought you to the conclusion that the camshaft is the problem?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-18-2000||11:24 PM||||I think she means the crank shaft pulley.<P>The crank won't turn or you can't get the bolt out? As I recall the bolt has normal thread but it's extremely tight. You need a very long wrench or an air wrench to get the main bolt out of the crank.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Babygirl||09-19-2000||01:33 AM||||This is Babygirl's husband :-)  She was listening to what I was saying but didn't hear everything quite right but she is learning :-)<P>I looked in the oil filler hole and saw that the rocker arms were not moving when the engine was turning over so I tore the valve cover off(4 cyl.).  I inspected them all to see if maybe I had busted the crank but none of them were moving.  This pointed to me the timing gear.<P>I removed the timing gear cover and the timing gear teeth are all broken and stripped :-(  Major bummer.  I have not removed the engine.<P>My next question is this... Can I get that timing gear off of the camshaft without pulling the engine?  If not do I have to take the camshaft in to, to have the gear pressed off and the new one pressed on?<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||5
Z||000005||Rodrv6||09-19-2000||04:39 PM||||There is a GM service bulletin that gives a procedure for removing the cam gear with the engine installed, but it involves drilling and tapping the end of the camshaft and using a puller to remove the gear.  You would probably be better off in the long run to remove the engine and pull the camshaft out.  The gear is pressed on and you will need to use a press.  I've gone through about 3 sets over the years and finally got a set of Pontiac super duty gears.  They are not cheap, but they are all metal and should last forever.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||4
Z||000006||Brian84SE||09-19-2000||08:20 PM||||Yes, apparently you can replace it without removing the engine. Try this link:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/timing-gear.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/timing-gear.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Babygirl||09-19-2000||10:57 PM||||Thanks Brian 84SE!  That link is awesome!  I'm buying a new METAL gear tomorrow, and replacing the gear.  While I'm under the hood, or the car as it seems, I'm going to fix the exhaust leak.  Thanks for the info!<P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||14
Z||000008||theogre||09-19-2000||11:07 PM||||These people have a puller kit for the gears that will do it in the car they claim. I don't know much about it. I just know they have the kit and I've heard people say it works. <A HREF="http://www.pontiacfiero.com/" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Knowledge Base</A><P>These guys have an article about it. <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Michigan Fiero Club</A><P>||||reg||1
